ow, we need to find the smallest possible value of |z - 2i|.\n\nLet z = a + bi, where a and b are real numbers.\n\n|z - 2i| = $\\sqrt{(a - 2)^2 + (b - 2)^2}$\n化小\nWe want to minimize this expression.\n\nAs mentioned earlier, all complex numbers will satisfy the initial equation, so we can choose any complex number that we like.\n\nTo simplify things, we can choose z to be a real number, a = x, where x is a real number.\n\nIf we choose z = 2 + 0i, we will have |z - 2i| = |2 - 2i| = $\\sqrt{4 + 0} = 2$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of |z - 2i| is 2.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\n$|2\\text{-}yi|_{min} = \\boxed{2}$",
